Thread title: [0.98a] Slay the Sector v0.5.3 (beta)

[center][img width=800]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PaulRouss3l/slay_the_sector/main/docs/assets/banner.png[/img]
[i]A Slay the Spire style roguelite, played inside your Starsector campaign.[/i]

[img width=800]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PaulRouss3l/slay_the_sector/main/docs/assets/node-map.png?v=2[/img]
[i]Every Act is a branching map of beacons: pick your path to the Boss.[/i]

[url=https://trilink.wispborne.com/open.html?mod=%7B%22url%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fraw.githubusercontent.com%2FPaulRouss3l%2Fslay_the_sector%2Fmain%2Fslay_the_sector.version%22%2C%22id%22%3A%22slay_the_sector%22%7D][img]https://trilink.wispborne.com/badges/install-badge-forthebadge.svg[/img][/url]

[size=12pt][b][url=https://github.com/PaulRouss3l/slay_the_sector/releases/download/v0.5.3/slay-the-sector-0.5.3.zip]Download v0.5.3 (beta)[/url][/b][/size]
[url=https://github.com/PaulRouss3l/slay_the_sector]Source code on GitHub[/url] | [url=https://github.com/PaulRouss3l/slay_the_sector/releases]All releases[/url]

[b]Requires:[/b] Starsector 0.98a. [b]No other mods needed.[/b][/center]

[hr]

[size=12pt][b]Save compatibility[/b][/size]
[list]
[li][b]Can be added to an ongoing game:[/b] yes. The Descent Relay appears the next time you load.[/li]
[li][b]Your campaign is safe:[/b] a Run changes nothing except a credit Payout at the end. XP, skills, story points, marines, reputation, bounties, cargo and salaries are all restored.[/li]
[li][b]Can be removed:[/b] [color=orange]not yet.[/color] A save that has used the mod needs it to load. Finish your Run and keep a backup before uninstalling.[/li]
[li][b]Other mods:[/b] compatible. Modded factions and ships show up as playable factions and as enemies. Tested with Nexerelin, Random Assortment of Things, Combat Chatter, MagicLib, LazyLib, LunaLib and GraphicsLib.[/li]
[/list]

[hr]

[size=12pt][b]What is it?[/b][/size]
The Descent Relay has opened somewhere in the core worlds. Dock with it, plug into its combat simulation, and fight your way down [b]The Descent[/b]: three Acts of branching battles, shops, events and Bosses, with a fleet you build as you go. Your real fleet waits safely at the Relay. When the Run ends, win or lose, you get it back exactly as you left it, plus a credit Payout for how deep you went.

[center][img width=800]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PaulRouss3l/slay_the_sector/main/docs/assets/intel-descent-relay.png?v=2[/img]
[i]The Descent Relay calls you from the Intel screen: Show on map, Lay in course.[/i][/center]

[b]How a Run plays[/b]
[list]
[li][b]Find the Relay:[/b] the Intel screen has it under Important, with Show on map and Lay in course.[/li]
[li][b]Pick a faction and a fleet:[/b] any faction with enough ships, modded ones included. Spend 30 DP on its ships, or press Random.[/li]
[li][b]Choose your path:[/b] every Act is a map of beacons. Pick the next one, fly there, and see what waits.[/li]
[li][b]Grow your fleet:[/b] after each win, take a ship, an officer or weapons. Supplies are the only currency, so repairs, shops and fleet size all compete for them.[/li]
[li][b]Beat the Boss:[/b] each Act ends with one. Win, choose a Boss reward, and descend deeper.[/li]
[/list]

[center][img width=800]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PaulRouss3l/slay_the_sector/main/docs/assets/reward-pick.png?v=2[/img]
[i]After each win, pick a ship, an officer or weapons. Watch the fleet's DP cap.[/i][/center]

[spoiler=What you can meet in the Descent]
[list]
[li][b]Combat:[/b] a standard fight. Win for supplies and a Reward pick.[/li]
[li][b]Elite:[/b] a stronger fleet surrounds you. Break out with most of your fleet.[/li]
[li][b]Ambush:[/b] the enemy runs. Destroy its marked flagship before it escapes.[/li]
[li][b]Events:[/b] a battle station (assault it or trade with it), sabotage, a side battle where you pick who to help, a convoy raid.[/li]
[li][b]Shop:[/b] ships, weapons, officers, repairs, D-mod removal and a bigger fleet cap, all paid in supplies. Shops grow with each Act.[/li]
[li][b]Rest:[/b] a free repair, an S-mod, an officer level, or removing a ship's D-mods.[/li]
[li][b]Treasure:[/b] one rare prize.[/li]
[li][b]Boss:[/b] the end of each Act. Its reward: an extra S-mod slot and an S-mod, a bigger fleet, or a Remnant warship.[/li]
[/list]
[/spoiler]

[spoiler=Progression: Ascension and Records]
Winning a Run unlocks harder levels for that faction, from Gamma to Omega (named after the AI cores of vanilla and Random Assortment of Things). Each level adds a handicap and a bigger Payout. Omega hides one last fight.
Your Records and three small starting bonuses are kept across all your saves.
[/spoiler]

[center][img width=800]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PaulRouss3l/slay_the_sector/main/docs/assets/act1-boss.png?v=2[/img]
[i]Each Act ends with a Boss. No retreat.[/i][/center]

[hr]

[size=12pt][b]This is a beta[/b][/size]
Everything in the mod works, but it is still being polished:
[list]
[li][b]Balance is not finished.[/b] Some fights may feel too hard or too easy, and some prices too cheap or too expensive. Your feedback is exactly what will fix that.[/li]
[li][b]Bugs are possible,[/b] especially in the later Acts, which have had less play time.[/li]
[/list]
[b]Found a problem, or something felt off?[/b] Please tell me! The easiest way is the [url=https://github.com/PaulRouss3l/slay_the_sector/issues/new/choose]Report a problem page[/url] on GitHub: pick "Report a bug" or "Balance feedback", and a short form guides you (you only need a free GitHub account). Describe what happened in your own words. If you can, drag and drop the file [b]starsector.log[/b] from your Starsector folder into the form: it helps a lot.
Replies in this thread are welcome too.

Most numbers (difficulty, rewards, prices, map shape) can also be changed in [b]data/config/settings.json[/b], if you like to tinker.

[hr]

[spoiler=Changelog]
[b]0.5.3 (beta)[/b]
[list]
[li]With Crew Stations installed, your first won Run also unlocks its Simulator Bay; the Run-end report says so.[/li]
[li]Nexerelin: Run fights no longer touch your real reputation, and the Descent's factions keep their relations.[/li]
[li]Credits other mods pay into the Run fleet during a Run (e.g. Nexerelin insurance) no longer leak into your campaign.[/li]
[li]The Descent's star system now sits inside the Sector's bounds (fixes skewed MagicLib bounty distances). Older saves are moved on load.[/li]
[li]Automated factions (e.g. Dustkeepers, once met) are playable: drones need no skill, an all-drone fleet gets a Command Uplink on its flagship.[/li]
[/list]

[b]0.5.2 (beta)[/b]
[list]
[li]Fixed a crash when confirming the Starting pick with Combat Chatter installed.[/li]
[li]Fixed a related error with Nexerelin's salvage scavenger dialog near the Run fleet.[/li]
[/list]

[b]0.5.1 (beta)[/b]
[i]Balance[/i]
[list]
[li]Act 2 and Act 3 no longer start easier than the end of the previous Act: fights climb from the previous Act's last fight.[/li]
[li]Supply rewards grow with the Act (x1.0 / x1.5 / x2.0), since the fleet gets bigger and costs more to repair.[/li]
[li]The true Boss and the battle station now start at full combat readiness.[/li]
[/list]
[i]Shops[/i]
[list]
[li]One page of stock per Act (Act 2 = 2 pages, Act 3 = 3 pages).[/li]
[li]Buy +10 Fleet DP cap for 100 supplies (first card of every Shop).[/li]
[/list]
[i]Interface[/i]
[list]
[li]Ship cards: hover a ship's name to see its fit, press F1 for its weapons, fighters and hullmods.[/li]
[li]The end of a Run posts an intel report with a notification: result, Payout, how deep you went, and what you unlocked.[/li]
[/list]
[i]Other[/i]
[list]
[li]Debug commands for the Console Commands mod: sts status, sts unlock, sts act 2-4, sts supplies (handy to test Act 4).[/li]
[li]The mod is now under the MIT license (LICENSE file included).[/li]
[li]Bug reports and balance feedback: friendly forms on the GitHub Issues page.[/li]
[/list]

[b]0.5.0 (beta)[/b]
First public release: three Acts, eight kinds of beacons, Shops, Rests, Treasures, Events, Boss rewards, Ascension levels and cross-save Records.

Full history in the [url=https://github.com/PaulRouss3l/slay_the_sector/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md]changelog[/url].
[/spoiler]

